    {
      "id": 66483,
      "name": "DrScott",
      "username": "DrScott",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/97f17d/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2013-06-26T01:03:43.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"BlueHairedMeerkat\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bluehairedmeerkat/48/1967_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> BlueHairedMeerkat:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Sounds like you played it pretty much right; I think you put the fowl into play one at a time, but once they've been knocked back out they don't get a second in.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I disagree, because destroyed cards go to the trash. &nbsp;So if you pulled each fowl out and put it into play individually, it would trigger Shopping, get destroyed, go to the trash and then come back out. &nbsp;That would trigger the infinite loop.</p>\n<p>The only way to avoid that is to follow the \"put <em>all </em>Fowl cards\" into play but doing it all at once. &nbsp;Then that card is done. &nbsp;Then Shopping Trip deals a one damage attack for each Fowl card that came out.</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:44:11.685Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
      "yours": false,
