    {
      "id": 66484,
      "name": "Katsue",
      "username": "Katsue",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/katsue/{size}/2012_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-06-26T06:42:03.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"DrScott\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/97f17d/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> DrScott:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>BlueHairedMeerkat wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Sounds like you played it pretty much right; I think you put the fowl into play one at a time, but once they've been knocked back out they don't get a second in.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\n&nbsp;I disagree, because destroyed cards go to the trash. &nbsp;So if you pulled each fowl out and put it into play individually, it would trigger Shopping, get destroyed, go to the trash and then come back out. &nbsp;That would trigger the infinite loop.The only way to avoid that is to follow the \"put <em>all </em>Fowl cards\" into play but doing it all at once. &nbsp;Then that card is done. &nbsp;Then Shopping Trip deals a one damage attack for each Fowl card that came out.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>If you look at the wording of Darken the Skies, and then take the rules in the rulebook into consideration, you take them all out of the trash one at a time, then you put them into play one at a time.</p>",
